  "stem": "The function \\(f\\) is defined by \\(f(x) = 3(x - 2)^{2} + 1\\). If \\(f(a) = 28\\) and \\(a > 2\\), what is the value of \\(a\\)?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "spr",
  "choices": null,
  "answer": null,
  "spr_answers": [
    "5"
  ],
  "solution": [
    "Set \\(3(a - 2)^{2} + 1 = 28\\), so \\(3(a - 2)^{2} = 27\\) and \\((a - 2)^{2} = 9\\).",
    "\\(a - 2 = 3\\) or \\(a - 2 = -3\\), so \\(a = 5\\) or \\(a = -1\\).",
    "Since \\(a > 2\\), \\(a = 5\\)."
  ],
  "explanation": null,
  "traps": null,
  "verify": "a = symbols('a')\nsols = solve(Eq(3*(a - 2)**2 + 1, 28), a)\nassert sorted(sols) == [-1, 5]\nassert [Rational(s) for s in spr_answers] == [s for s in sols if s > 2]",
